eliminate $A$ and solve for $B:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7(-1)-11 & =A(-1+1)+B(-1-8) \\\\ -18 & =-9B \\\\ B & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{7x-11}{(x-8)(x+1)}=\\frac{5}{x-8}+\\frac{2}{x+1}.\n$$\n\nFinally, we integrate, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{7x-11}{(x-8)(x+1)}\\,\\text{d}x & =5\\int \\frac{1}{x-8}\\,\\text{d}x+2\\int \\frac{1}{x+1}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =5\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-8|+2\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+1|+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535077 true] [17592186329990 1000 #edb/ref 17592186329991 13194139535077 true] [17592186329990 1000 #edb/ref 17592186329992 13194139535077 true] [17592186329990 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139535077 true] [17592186329990 1041 "field-1" 13194139535077 true] [17592186329990 1104 #edb/ref 17592186329992 13194139535077 true] [17592186329990 1110 #uuid "19e6f951-0205-55ba-824c-bc46c458c916" 13194139535077 true] [17592186329991 1034 "4" 13194139535077 true] [17592186329991 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535077 true] [17592186329991 1111 #uuid "f9c952b5-b0b8-5452-8c02-cc50c1112f68" 13194139535077 true] [17592186329992 1034 "5" 13194139535077 true] [17592186329992 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535077 true] [17592186329992 1111 #uuid "9313535f-7431-5830-bd3d-58895013ec28" 13194139535077 true] [17592186329993 1000 #edb/ref 17592186329994 13194139535077 true] [17592186329993 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139535077 true] [17592186329993 1041 "field-2" 13194139535077 true] [17592186329993 1104 #edb/ref 17592186329994 13194139535077 true] [17592186329993 1110 #uuid "08ee7f52-3d9e-53df-8993-e91d3408c9c2" 13194139535077 true] [17592186329994 1034 "2" 13194139535077 true] [17592186329994 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535077 true] [17592186329994 1111 #uuid "b34bcff9-df4c-5706-87b3-081d015c2a81" 13194139535077 true] [17592186329995 1017 #edb/ref 17592186329996 13194139535077 true] [17592186329995 1017 #edb/ref 17592186329998 13194139535077 true] [17592186329995 1089 "q-348933" 13194139535077 true] [17592186329995 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535077 true] [17592186329995 1100 "Evaluate the following indefinite integral and fill in the missing coefficients.\n\n$\\int \\frac{11}{(2x+5)(x-2)}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}$\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡|2x+5|\\,+\\,$\n{{field-2}}$\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-2|+C$" 13194139535077 true] [17592186329995 1113 #uuid "16dae2d4-d8c2-58dc-951e-8924c446f8fe" 13194139535077 true] [17592186329995 1145 "First, we note that the denominator of the integrand can be factored as\n\n$$\n(2x+5)(x-2).\n$$\n\nWe convert the integrand into a sum of partial fractions:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{11}{(2x+5)(x-2)} & =\\frac{A}{2x+5}+\\frac{B}{x-2},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich gives\n\n$$\n11=A(x-2)+B(2x+5).\n$$\n\nPlugging in $x=2,$ we can eliminate $A$ and solve for $B:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}11 & =9B \\\\ B & =\\frac{11}{9}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nOn the other hand, plugging in $x=-\\frac{5}{2},$ we can eliminate $B$ and solve for $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}11 & =-\\frac{9}{2}A \\\\ A & =-\\frac{22}{9}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{11}{(2x+5)(x-2)}=-\\frac{22}{9(2x+5)}+\\frac{11}{9(x-2)}.\n$$\n\nFinally, we integrate, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{11}{(2x+5)(x-2)}\\,\\text{d}x & =-\\frac{22}{9}\\int \\frac{1}{2x+5}\\,\\text{d}x+\\frac{11}{9}\\int \\frac{1}{x-2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{11}{9}\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡|2x+5|+\\frac{11}{9}\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-2|+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535077 true] [17592186329996 1000 #edb/ref 17592186329997 13194139535077 true] [17592186329996 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139535077 true] [17592186329996 1041 "field-1" 13194139535077 true] [17592186329996 1104 #edb/ref 17592186329997 13194139535077 true] [17592186329996 1110 #uuid "102cb884-e241-59e7-8d95-bc521e1d32c3" 13194139535077 true] [17592186329997 1034 "-\\frac{11}{9}" 13194139535077 true] [17592186329997 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535077 true] [17592186329997 1111 #uuid "d7cb62f1-624b-5572-8b9d-2e57dd7cb8d8" 13194139535077 true] [17592186329998 1000 #edb/ref 17592186329999 13194139535077 true] [17592186329998 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139535077 true] [17592186329998 1041 "field-2" 13194139535077 true] [17592186329998 1104 #edb/ref 17592186329999 13194139535077 true] [17592186329998 1110 #uuid "522f3f76-4d45-55c6-9c0d-f0605d17a519" 13194139535077 true] [17592186329999 1034 "\\frac{11}{9}" 13194139535077 true] [17592186329999 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535077 true] [17592186329999 1111 #uuid "07099bbf-40db-554d-af1a-de896fb2e589" 13194139535077 true] [17592186330000 1017 #edb/ref 17592186330001 13194139535077 true] [17592186330000 1089 "q-348976" 13194139535077 true] [17592186330000 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139535077 true] [17592186330000 1100 "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{-4}^{0}\\frac{5x-1}{{x}^{2}+4x-5}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139535077 true] [17592186330000 1113 #uuid "90a8232e-fe3a-5d08-9a00-221f3761736e" 13194139535077 true] [17592186330000 1145 "We'll work out the indefinite integral first and then proceed with the definite integral.\n\nFirst, we note that the denominator of the integrand can be factored as\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}+4x-5=(x+5)(x-1).\n$$\n\nSo the integrand can be converted into a sum of partial fractions,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5x-1}{{x}^{2}+4x-5} & =\\frac{5x-1}{(x+5)(x-1)}=\\frac{A}{x+5}+\\frac{B}{x-1},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich gives\n\n$$\n5x-1=A(x-1)+B(x+5).\n$$\n\nPlugging in $x=1,$ we can eliminate $A$ and solve for $B:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5(1)-1 & =A(1-1)+B(1+5) \\\\ 4 & =6B \\\\ B & =\\frac{2}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nOn the other hand, plugging in $x=-5,$ we can eliminate $B$ and solve for $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5(-5)-1 & =A(-5-1)+B(-5+5) \\\\ -26 & =-6A \\\\ A & =\\frac{13}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{5x-1}{{x}^{2}+4x-5}=\\frac{13}{3(x+5)}+\\frac{2}{3(x-1)}.\n$$\n\nNow, we integrate, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{5x-1}{{x}^{2}+4x-5}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (\\frac{13}{3(x+5)}+\\frac{2}{3(x-1)})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{13}{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+5|+\\frac{2}{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-1|+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can simplify the result using the laws of logarithms, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{5x-1}{{x}^{2}+4x-5}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{13}{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+5|+\\frac{2}{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-1|+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the definite integral is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-4}^{0}\\frac{5x-1}{{x}^{2}+4x-5}\\,\\text{d}x & ={[\\frac{13}{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+5|+\\frac{2}{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-1|]}_{-4}^{0} \\\\  & =(\\frac{13}{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5)+\\frac{2}{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1))-(\\frac{13}{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1)+\\frac{2}{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5)) \\\\  & =\\frac{13}{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5)-\\frac{2}{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5) \\\\  & =\\frac{11}{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5).\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535077 true] [17592186330001 1000 #edb/ref 17592186330002 13194139535077 true] [17592186330001 1000 #edb/ref 17592186330003 13194139535077 true] [17592186330001 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139535077 true] [17592186330001 1041 "field-1" 13194139535077 true] [17592186330001 1104 #edb/ref 17592186330002 13194139535077 true] [17592186330001 1110 #uuid "26f01bd9-0772-5dd9-979c-19468dbb5bd4" 13194139535077 true] [17592186330002 1034 "\\frac{11}{3}\\ln(5)" 13194139535077 true] [17592186330002 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535077 true] [17592186330002 1111 #uuid "483f7011-c7aa-512d-87b8-a19f9958a524" 13194139535077 true] [17592186330003 1034 "\\ln(5)" 13194139535077 true] [17592186330003 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535077 true] [17592186330003 1111 #uuid "460331c6-d06c-57b0-8fd2-3ca938fc55fb" 13194139535077 true] [17592186330004 1017 #edb/ref 17592186330005 13194139535077 true] [17592186330004 1089 "q-349040" 13194139535077 true] [17592186330004 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139535077 true] [17592186330004 1100 "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{\\frac{1}{2}}\\frac{36x-10}{12{x}^{2}-x-6}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139535077 true] [17592186330004 1113 #uuid "047f5aca-d84b-5888-b35a-81b77ae7adbc" 13194139535077 true] [17592186330004 1145 "We'll work out the indefinite integral first and then proceed with the definite integral.\n\nFirst, we note that a denominator of the integrand can be factored as\n\n$$\n12{x}^{2}-x-6=(4x-3)(3x+2).\n$$\n\nSo the integrand can be converted into a sum of partial fractions,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{36x-10}{12{x}^{2}-x-6} & =\\frac{36x-10}{(4x-3)(3x+2)}=\\frac{A}{4x-3}+\\frac{B}{3x+2},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich gives\n\n$$\n36x-10=A(3x+2)+B(4x-3).\n$$\n\nPlugging in $x=\\frac{3}{4},$ we can eliminate $B$ and solve for $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}36(\\frac{3}{4})-10 & =A(3(\\frac{3}{4})+2)+B(4(\\frac{3}{4})-3) \\\\ 17 & =\\frac{17}{4}A \\\\ A & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nOn the other hand, plugging in $x=-\\frac{2}{3},$ we can eliminate $A$ and solve for $B:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}36(-\\frac{2}{3})-10 & =A(3(-\\frac{2}{3})+2)+B(4(-\\frac{2}{3})-3) \\\\ -34 & =-\\frac{17}{3}B \\\\ B & =6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{36x-10}{12{x}^{2}-x-6}=\\frac{4}{4x-3}+\\frac{6}{3x+2}.\n$$\n\nNow, we integrate, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{36x-10}{12{x}^{2}-x-6}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (\\frac{4}{4x-3}+\\frac{6}{3x+2})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡|4x-3|+2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|3x+2|+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can simplify the result using the laws of logarithms, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{36x-10}{12{x}^{2}-x-6}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡|4x-3|+2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|3x+2|+C \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡|(4x-3)(3x+2)^{2}|+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the definite integral is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\frac{1}{2}}\\frac{36x-10}{12{x}^{2}-x-6}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡|(4x-3)(3x+2)^{2}|{|}_{0}^{\\frac{1}{2}} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{49}{4})-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(12) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{49}{48}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{49}{48}).\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535077 true] [17592186330005 1000 #edb/ref 17592186330006 13194139535077 true] [17592186330005 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139535077 true] [17592186330005 1041 "field-1" 13194139535077 true] [17592186330005 1104 #edb/ref 17592186330006 13194139535077 true] [17592186330005 1110 #uuid "6228426c-c1df-5f2b-b917-c412d67493dc" 13194139535077 true] [17592186330006 1034 "\\ln(\\frac{49}{48})" 13194139535077 true] [17592186330006 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535077 true] [17592186330006 1111 #uuid "3cfb5d8c-8454-5d20-9a85-a0ce83e2d18a" 13194139535077 true] [17592186330007 1034 "\\ln(\\frac{2}{121})" 13194139535077 true] [17592186330007 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535077 true] [17592186330007 1111 #uuid "e131523c-815a-54eb-8aac-8845ae79f21d" 13194139535077 true] [17592186330008 1017 #edb/ref 17592186330009 13194139535077 true] [17592186330008 1089 "q-49764" 13194139535077 true] [17592186330008 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535077 true] [17592186330008 1100 "${\\int }_{-6}^{-5}\\frac{5x+29}{(x+7)(x+4)}\\,\\text{d}x=$" 13194139535077 true] [17592186330008 1113 #uuid "c679d3d1-b950-5f64-a26b-57b3e4e6ca7f" 13194139535077 true] [17592186330008 1145 "We'll work out the indefinite integral first and then proceed with the definite integral.\n\nFirst, we convert the integrand into a sum of partial fractions:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5x+29}{(x+7)(x+4)}=\\frac{A}{(x+7)}+\\frac{B}{(x+4)},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich gives\n\n$$\n5x+29=A(x+4)+B(x+7).\n$$\n\nPlugging in $x=-4,$ we can eliminate $A$ and solve for $B:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5(-4)+29 & =A(-4+4)+B(-4+7) \\\\ 9 & =3B \\\\ B & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nOn the other hand, plugging in $x=-7,$ we can eliminate $B$ and solve for $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5(-7)+29 & =A(-7+4)+B(-7+7) \\\\ -6 & 